{"id":"ethical-hacking","title":"Ethical hacking 101","subject":"Cybersecurity","label":"Cybersecurity","exams":[],"language":"en","seconds":170,"duration":169.51,"audio":"voice.mp3","words":460,"sections":[{"id":"hook","title":"Opening question","start":0,"end":14.565},{"id":"explain","title":"Permission first","start":14.565,"end":58.585},{"id":"explain2","title":"The law","start":58.585,"end":87.055},{"id":"example","title":"Worked example","start":87.055,"end":108.435},{"id":"check","title":"Quick check","start":108.435,"end":117.795},{"id":"answer","title":"The answer","start":117.795,"end":123.155},{"id":"mistakes","title":"Common slips","start":123.155,"end":141.075},{"id":"recap","title":"Recap","start":141.075,"end":169.51}],"lines":[{"s":0,"a":0.5,"b":4.58,"text":"Your friend dares you to peek at the school results system, just to look.","w":[0.54,0.78,1.1,1.4,1.6,1.76,2.06,2.16,2.32,2.66,3.08,3.92,4.22,4.32]},{"s":0,"a":4.88,"b":10.2,"text":"Is that harmless curiosity, or a crime? I'm Kora, and this is ethical hacking.","w":[4.92,5.02,5.22,5.66,6.58,6.72,6.84,7.86,8.1,8.96,9.1,9.3,9.48,9.82]},{"s":0,"a":10.5,"b":14.14,"text":"By the end, you'll know the safe, legal way to think like a defender.","w":[10.58,10.76,10.98,11.44,11.68,11.88,12.08,12.48,12.8,13.08,13.22,13.46,13.62,13.7]},{"s":1,"a":14.99,"b":21.93,"text":"An ethical hacker, also called a penetration tester or white hat, is paid to find weaknesses before criminals do.","w":[15.04,15.22,15.6,16.28,16.62,16.92,16.98,17.58,18.18,18.38,18.68,19.44,19.6,19.88,20,20.3,20.88,21.22,21.68]},{"s":1,"a":22.23,"b":25.21,"text":"They work only with written permission and an agreed scope.","w":[22.24,22.44,22.9,23.2,23.42,23.7,24.3,24.42,24.5,24.9]},{"s":1,"a":25.51,"b":28.82,"text":"Their job is to help the owner fix problems, not to show off.","w":[25.56,25.84,26.16,26.26,26.36,26.56,26.72,27.02,27.28,28.06,28.26,28.4,28.68]},{"s":1,"a":29.12,"b":36.03,"text":"That permission is what separates white hat from black hat. Black hats break in without permission, for harm or profit.","w":[29.14,29.4,29.88,29.98,30.18,30.8,31.08,31.36,31.54,31.82,32.68,32.98,33.28,33.58,33.72,34.06,34.92,35.12,35.5,35.64]},{"s":1,"a":36.33,"b":42.42,"text":"Grey hats may have good intent, but they act without permission. Permission and intent decide the label.","w":[36.4,36.72,37.04,37.22,37.38,37.58,38.28,38.44,38.74,38.92,39.22,40.26,40.9,41.06,41.58,41.98,42.1]},{"s":1,"a":42.72,"b":49.97,"text":"How do they think? Learn about the system, look for weak points, test them carefully, then report and help fix.","w":[42.78,42.94,43.06,43.22,44.18,44.46,44.68,44.82,45.62,45.86,46.04,46.28,47.06,47.32,47.5,48.44,48.66,49.12,49.24,49.48]},{"s":1,"a":50.27,"b":54.3,"text":"To start safely, learn networking, Linux, and a little programming.","w":[50.32,50.46,50.76,51.56,51.82,52.76,53.28,53.4,53.46,53.7]},{"s":1,"a":54.6,"b":58.16,"text":"Bug bounty programmes, with published rules, come later.","w":[54.74,55.02,55.38,56.2,56.46,56.86,57.62,57.84]},{"s":2,"a":59.01,"b":67.2,"text":"The law is simple. Accessing a computer without permission is a crime almost everywhere, even if you only look, and even as a joke.","w":[59.02,59.18,59.56,59.7,60.84,61.32,61.4,61.86,62.2,62.8,62.92,63.02,63.44,63.88,64.8,65,65.08,65.28,65.52,66.1,66.3,66.6,66.76,66.84]},{"s":2,"a":67.5,"b":71.58,"text":"A joke does not change the law. Curiosity does not create permission.","w":[67.56,67.68,68.02,68.26,68.54,68.88,69,69.72,70.44,70.64,70.84,71.14]},{"s":2,"a":71.88,"b":80.25,"text":"Examples include the Cybercrimes Act in Nigeria, the Computer Misuse Act in the United Kingdom, and the Computer Fraud and Abuse Act in the United States.","w":[71.98,72.5,72.82,72.96,73.72,73.96,74.06,75.14,75.28,75.7,76.18,76.36,76.44,76.56,76.88,77.62,77.72,77.82,78.28,78.58,78.68,79.08,79.26,79.34,79.44,79.78]},{"s":2,"a":80.55,"b":86.63,"text":"Touching systems without permission is illegal. Defending is legal when you have permission and stay inside the scope.","w":[80.6,80.98,81.4,81.72,82.26,82.4,83.32,83.9,84.06,84.4,84.56,84.72,84.94,85.48,85.64,85.92,86.24,86.36]},{"s":3,"a":87.48,"b":93.48,"text":"Back to the dare. You do not touch the school results system. Even looking is unauthorised access.","w":[87.48,87.72,87.82,87.94,88.64,88.78,88.92,89.14,89.46,89.58,89.9,90.3,91.34,91.58,91.98,92.2,92.96]},{"s":3,"a":93.78,"b":102.07,"text":"Instead, report the weakness to a teacher. Practise the same skill in a CTF, a capture the flag competition built for safe practice.","w":[93.84,94.5,94.86,94.96,95.36,95.52,95.58,96.48,96.94,97.12,97.48,97.9,98.02,98.14,99.16,99.28,99.66,99.78,100.1,100.74,101.04,101.22,101.52]},{"s":3,"a":102.37,"b":105.39,"text":"That gives you skill without breaking trust or the law.","w":[102.4,102.64,102.86,103.02,103.68,104.02,104.4,104.88,104.98,105.1]},{"s":3,"a":105.69,"b":108.01,"text":"If you are unsure, stop and ask.","w":[105.72,105.82,105.98,106.2,107.02,107.44,107.68]},{"s":4,"a":108.86,"b":115.09,"text":"Quick check. A company invites you to test its website and gives you written rules. Is that ethical hacking?","w":[108.9,109.16,109.88,110,110.44,110.82,110.94,111.08,111.4,111.56,112.28,112.42,112.66,112.82,113.1,113.84,113.94,114.22,114.6]},{"s":4,"a":115.54,"b":117.37,"text":"Pause here and try it. I'll wait.","w":[115.56,115.86,116.1,116.2,116.46,116.92,117.04]},{"s":5,"a":118.22,"b":122.73,"text":"Yes, because you have permission and a scope, so testing is legal and defensive.","w":[118.24,118.8,119.02,119.14,119.28,119.82,119.94,120,120.94,121.14,121.6,121.74,122.12,122.22]},{"s":6,"a":123.58,"b":128.91,"text":"One mistake is testing first and asking later. Get written permission before you touch anything.","w":[123.76,123.9,124.36,124.48,124.9,125.28,125.5,125.84,126.82,127.04,127.36,127.8,128.1,128.26,128.5]},{"s":6,"a":129.21,"b":134.23,"text":"Another is using a friend's account or device without clear permission. A favour is not a scope.","w":[129.3,129.72,129.9,130.16,130.26,130.54,130.94,131.04,131.44,131.82,132.08,133.08,133.2,133.58,133.72,133.92,133.98]},{"s":6,"a":134.53,"b":140.65,"text":"A third is practising on any live site. Use only CTFs, your own lab, or labs that invite you.","w":[134.62,134.74,135.04,135.18,135.72,135.92,136.12,136.44,137.54,137.74,138.06,138.72,138.98,139.16,139.52,139.68,140,140.18,140.48]},{"s":7,"a":141.5,"b":145.42,"text":"Ethical hackers find weaknesses with written permission and an agreed scope.","w":[141.58,141.96,142.44,142.72,143.26,143.42,143.7,144.42,144.54,144.64,145.04]},{"s":7,"a":145.72,"b":149.68,"text":"White, black, and grey hats differ by permission and intent.","w":[145.8,146.46,147.12,147.28,147.56,147.98,148.34,148.54,149.12,149.26]},{"s":7,"a":149.98,"b":159.34,"text":"Start with networking, Linux, and a little programming. Practise only on systems built to be attacked, and use bug bounty programmes with published rules later.","w":[150.06,150.36,150.58,151.58,152.28,152.42,152.52,152.8,153.88,154.42,154.68,154.84,155.28,155.52,155.64,155.76,156.66,156.88,157.08,157.32,157.62,158.1,158.28,158.66,159.02]},{"s":7,"a":159.64,"b":164.68,"text":"Top tip: learn defence alongside attack, and keep every test inside written rules.","w":[159.66,159.98,160.68,160.96,161.4,161.94,162.56,162.7,163.02,163.28,163.64,164.04,164.3]},{"s":7,"a":164.98,"b":168.91,"text":"Knowzone is here to help you learn safely, one clear step at a time.","w":[165.06,165.54,165.66,165.86,165.96,166.14,166.3,166.6,167.7,167.92,168.2,168.44,168.54,168.6]}],"scenes":[{"at":0.25,"heading":"Opening question","items":[{"at":0.4,"kind":"text","text":"Friend dares you to peek at results system"},{"at":4.78,"kind":"text","text":"Harmless curiosity or a crime?"},{"at":10.4,"kind":"text","text":"Learn safe, legal defender mindset"}]},{"at":14.74,"heading":"Permission first","items":[{"at":14.89,"kind":"term","text":"Ethical hacker","detail":"Penetration tester/white hat; paid to find weaknesses first"},{"at":22.13,"kind":"text","text":"Written permission and agreed scope"},{"at":25.41,"kind":"text","text":"Help owner fix, not show off"},{"at":29.02,"kind":"term","text":"Black hat","detail":"No permission; harm or profit"},{"at":36.23,"kind":"term","text":"Grey hat","detail":"Good intent, but no permission; permission and intent decide label"}]},{"at":42.47,"heading":"Think like a defender","items":[{"at":42.62,"kind":"text","text":"Learn, find weak points, test, report, fix"},{"at":50.17,"kind":"text","text":"Start: networking, Linux, programming"},{"at":54.5,"kind":"text","text":"Bug bounties with published rules later"}]},{"at":58.76,"heading":"The law","items":[{"at":58.91,"kind":"text","text":"No permission = crime, even just looking"},{"at":67.4,"kind":"text","text":"Joke or curiosity does not create permission"},{"at":71.78,"kind":"text","text":"Cybercrimes Act (NG), Computer Misuse Act (UK), CFAA (US)"},{"at":80.45,"kind":"text","text":"Defending legal: permission and inside scope"}]},{"at":87.23,"heading":"Worked example: the dare","items":[{"at":87.38,"kind":"text","text":"Don't touch; even looking = unauthorised"},{"at":93.68,"kind":"text","text":"Report to teacher; practise in a CTF"},{"at":102.27,"kind":"text","text":"Skill without breaking trust or law"},{"at":105.59,"kind":"text","text":"Unsure? Stop and ask."}]},{"at":108.44,"heading":"Quick check","items":[{"at":108.44,"kind":"question","text":"A company invites you to test its website and gives you written rules. Is that ethical hacking?"}]},{"at":117.97,"heading":"Answer","items":[{"at":118.12,"kind":"term","text":"Permission","detail":"Written permission and agreed scope"},{"at":118.12,"kind":"text","text":"Yes: legal and defensive"}]},{"at":123.33,"heading":"Common slips","items":[{"at":123.48,"kind":"wrong","text":"Test first, ask later"},{"at":129.11,"kind":"wrong","text":"Use friend's account/device without clear permission"},{"at":134.43,"kind":"wrong","text":"Practise on any live site"}]},{"at":141.25,"heading":"Recap","items":[{"at":141.4,"kind":"text","text":"Find weaknesses: written permission and scope"},{"at":145.62,"kind":"text","text":"White/black/grey differ by permission and intent"},{"at":149.88,"kind":"text","text":"Start: networking, Linux, programming"},{"at":149.88,"kind":"text","text":"Practise only on systems built to be attacked"},{"at":149.88,"kind":"text","text":"Bug bounties with published rules later"}]},{"at":159.39,"heading":"Top tip","items":[{"at":159.54,"kind":"tip","text":"Learn defence alongside attack; keep every test inside written rules."},{"at":164.88,"kind":"text","text":"Knowzone: learn safely, one clear step at a time."}]}],"check":{"at":117.62,"seconds":10,"question":"A company invites you to test its website and gives you written rules. Is that ethical hacking?","answer":"Yes — permission and scope make testing legal and defensive."},"fps":30,"mouth":"","level":"","credits":[],"voice":"qwen3-tts-12hz-1.7b (cloned voice)"}